      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, i need help writing a rejection email for a candidate. They made it to the final round for a senior dev role here in Austin, so it's a tough one. They were really strong in system design and had great culture fit, but we just went with someone who had a bit more experience with our specific cloud stack. Can you draft something professional and kind so we don't burn a bridge?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's a draft rejection email that balances professionalism with kindness:\n\nDear [Candidate Name],\n\nI wanted to personally reach out to you regarding the status of your application for the Senior Developer role at [Company Name]. We were truly impressed by your exceptional system design skills and your alignment with our company culture. However, after careful consideration, we have decided to move forward with another candidate whose experience with our specific cloud stack aligns more closely with our current needs.\n\nPlease know that this decision was not made lightly, and we were genuinely excited about the prospect of having you join our team. Your passion for system design and your fit with our company culture were evident throughout the interview process, and we appreciate the time and effort you invested in sharing your qualifications with us.\n\nAs a seasoned developer, you're likely no stranger to navigating complex technical landscapes, and I'm sure you'll find another opportunity that's a perfect fit for your skills and experience. We're confident that your talents will be in high demand, and we wish you all the best in your job search.\n\nIf you have any questions or concerns, please don't hesitate to reach out. We appreciate your interest in [Company Name] and hope to have the opportunity to work with you in the future.\n\nBest",
